// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'psk'
//
// `# Kerberos { psk: 'abcde'; }#` -- a Kerberos authentication island with a body. The rule
// for this island is literally `EOF`: it takes no fields at all, and the only spelling that
// parses is the empty `# Kerberos { }#` in ../fixtures/t2-authentication.pure.
//
// An island type with a mandatory-empty body is the one shape a rewrite has no reason to
// implement. Islands are parsed by dispatching the body text to a registered sub-parser, and
// the natural degenerate case -- no fields, so nothing to parse, so accept anything and build
// the empty object -- is exactly the wrong one. The field written here is borrowed from the
// PSK island next door, so it is a real field of a real authentication kind in the same
// grammar, dispatched by name.
//
// This is also the boundary that makes `authentication:` islands parseable at all: the body is
// handed to AuthenticationGrammarParserExtension by KIND, so the kind name alone decides which
// fields exist. Get the dispatch table right and get the empty case wrong, and every Kerberos
// connection in the corpus still parses.
###Connection
MongoDBConnection fixture::neg::KerberosWithBody
{
  database: legend_db;
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  serverURLs: [localhost:27017];
  authentication: # Kerberos {
    psk: 'abcde';
  }#;
}
